SUMMARY:Pom Poko (1994)
LOCATION:The Cinemagic Theater\, 2021 SE Hawthorne Blvd\, Portland OR
GEO:45.5122;-122.6366
DESCRIPTION:Dir. Isao Takahata · 119 min\n\nThe Raccoons of the Tama Hills
  are being forced from their homes by the rapid development of houses and 
 shopping malls. As it becomes harder to find food and shelter\, they decid
 e to band together and fight back. The Raccoons practice and perfect the a
 ncient art of transformation until they are even able to appear as humans 
 in hilarious circumstances.\n\nTickets: https://tickets.thecinemagictheate
 r.com/checkout/showing/pom-poko-sub/4116561/\n\nMore showtimes: https://ma
 ttlohkamp.github.io/small-screens-pdx/
